+JSON in, JSON out. Routes are listed in `README.md`; `GET /audit` lists the
+audit log (below).
+
+## Keys and roles
+
+Every request carries an API key: `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys are
+kept in the data (`apiKeys`, see `docs/DATA.md`), each with a role:
+
+- `viewer` may only read (every `GET` except `/audit`).
+- `cook` may also cook recipes (`POST /recipes/:id/cook`), record waste
+  (`POST /batches/:id/waste`), log temperatures (`POST /temperatures`) and
+  enter stock-take counts (`POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`).
+- `manager` may do everything, including `GET /audit`.
+
+A request without a key, or with an unknown key, gets 401 `unauthorized`. A
+known key without the needed role gets 403 `forbidden`.
+
+## Audit log
+
+Every request that changes data (any method but `GET`) made with a known key
+is recorded, whatever its outcome:
+`{ "id", "at", "key", "method", "path", "status" }`, where `key` is the key's
+name, never the key itself. `GET /audit` (managers only) lists the entries
+newest first.

